  "hypothesis": "Current glyph validation spends repeated instructions extracting and sign-extending four coordinates before two ordered bounds comparisons. Use one packed signed-short comparison on the same already-loaded eight bytes. Current profile locates glyphvalidation;its libc samples do not isolate copy cost. No CPU gain forecast from sample counts.",
  "intendedEndState": "SSE2 shifts the existing loaded bounds by4bytes and compares the two low signedshort lanes in parallel. MoveMask&15 observes only ymin>ymax and xmin>xmax. Original scalar expression is the guarded portable fallback;no new scalar policy or validation change. Keep originaltyped loca loop instead of the inconclusive extent prototype.",
  "proof": "The big-endian UInt64 has words xmin,ymin,xmax,ymax from most to least significant. Vector128.CreateScalar gives low signed lanes ymax,xmax,ymin,xmin. Shifting4bytes gives ymin,xmin in the low two lanes. Signed CompareGreaterThan produces exactly the original two failure predicates;mask15 discards upper lanes and checks both bytes of each observed lane. Existing10byte header extent/zero-contour policy and same UInt64 read remain before this predicate. Every glyph poll/order/location/header/mapping failure and original scalar fallback are preserved. Reverse transformations reconstruct entire accepted source;allunlisted production bodies verbatim.",
